The records of D3.1 for two and for three recipes on one Mac (docs/plans/v0.1.md, D6), built directly
and not by an install: an install refuses a second recipe (BD14), but the records stay per recipe, and
T24 (three recipes, each failing in its own way) and T30 (one recipe's disk rule never removes a file
another recipe's descriptor names) need them. Each folder is a data root's records and files, written
once by U2 (2026-11-27) with fixed ids that match A2's patterns; no id here is ever minted again.

  two/     recipes A and B
  three/   recipes A, B and C: two/ byte for byte, and C's folder with the three files only C names

Git keeps neither modes nor empty folders, so a test copies one with tests/helpers.sh `records_fixture
two|three DEST`, which gives every folder mode 0700 (and each recipe its kept/ and failed/), every record
0600 and every file in store/ 0444, as Auster leaves them. T0 checks that every record reads with
common/auster's readers, that every sha256 a descriptor names is a file in store/ with that sha256, that
each launch line names its engine's file list by its sha256, that every file in store/ is named by a
descriptor, and that two/ is three/ less C.

The ids
  rapdsanqlj2eu  recipe A                       rkfbt7hbg4kzw  recipe B
  r6xnosrsvgruc  recipe C (three/ only)
  ecmk3usbjhyrc  engine b12359                  ew6sxpf27zvlg  engine b12400 (made up)
  mkvfeqqxoygjg  model A, the older file        macehkwh77vhw  model A
  mx2o3cznfz23s  model B
  byvlad4zog2kq  A's earlier build              bm4smkutoesko  A's build in use
  bvuefucqhcs35  A's build that failed          bnkj6d7jgrlzs  B's earlier build
  bjhl5vv2hfgyg  B's build in use               bx33a5rua3kky  C's build in use

The descriptors (engine, model, template, system prompt, test, each by the first 8 hex digits of its
sha256; then people, context per person, port and speed)

