What they share, which is what T30 is about:
- model A's older file (f266677f) is named by A's kept entry and by B's serving: removing A's earlier
  build must leave it;
- engine b12400 (086ad00d) is named by A's failed entry, B's kept entry and, in three/, C's serving;
- engine b12359 (5aad25b2) is named by A's serving, A's kept entry and B's serving;
- model B (f542df1e) is named by B's kept entry and, in three/, C's serving.
Each recipe has its own template, system prompt and test, since a build is named by one recipe's order
lines only (A3).

The other records
  builds/mac           a 64 GB Mac (GPU limit 53,084 MiB), macOS 27.2.1, router 0a:1b:2c:3d:4e:5f, no keep-awake
  builds/local-name    test-mac, the stub scutil's LocalHostName
  builds/<A>/hold      A's failed build, bvuefucqhcs35, held
  builds/<r>/start     each recipe: starting, at 10.0.0.5, a fixed boot session, time 1800000000

store/ holds each file a descriptor names, as text that says what it stands for: the engine archives
("engine archive stand-in, b12359"), the models ("model stand-in A"), templates, system prompts and
tests. engines/<sha256>/ holds each engine "unpacked": root/llama-stub/llama-server, a stand-in that only
exits 1, and files, its list in the form of B3 step 9, whose sha256 the launch lines name (36799637 for
b12359, 74d40bde for b12400). Nothing here is ever run.
